IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cla2-common`

-- Civil Liability Act 2002 (WA) -- baseline-2026-11: s 13A (damages for care needs while in the catastrophic injuries
-- support scheme, CISS) and Part 2 Division 4 (structured settlements, ss 14-15).
--
-- SEAT. The injured person claiming personal injury damages. Every question is asked as that person would ask it.
--
-- Borrowed terms, asked as facts: whether the person is a "lifetime participant" or an "interim participant" in the CISS,
-- and what a "motor vehicle injury" or "workplace injury" is, are the Motor Vehicle and Workplace Accidents (Catastrophic
-- Injuries) Act 2016's (s 13A(1), (2)).
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Part 2 Divisions 3 and 4 -- care needs in the CISS, and structured settlements`

§§ `s 13A -- damages for my care needs while I am in the CISS`

DECLARE `My injury` IS ONE OF
    `a motor vehicle injury`
    `a workplace injury`
    `another injury`

DECLARE `My place in the CISS` IS ONE OF
    `I am a lifetime participant for this injury`
    `I am an interim participant for this injury`
    `I was an interim participant, stopped being one, and did not become a lifetime participant`
    `I have never been a participant for this injury`

DECLARE `When the care needs arise` IS ONE OF
    `while I am, or was, a participant`
    `in the future: they will or may arise`
    `before I became a participant`

-- s 13A(1): "treatment, care and support needs" are those defined in the MVWA(CI) Act s 3(1), including excluded ones; (3):
-- "it includes gratuitous services of a domestic nature or ... nursing and attendance" by family or household; (9): whether
-- or not assessed, paid for by the Commission, or given free.
-- (4), (5): for "a motor vehicle injury or workplace injury suffered by a person if the person is a participant in the CISS
-- in respect of the injury", "No damages can be awarded to the person in respect of any treatment, care and support needs of
-- the person that relate to the motor vehicle injury or workplace injury and that -- (a) have arisen during the period in
-- respect of which the person is a participant in the CISS; or (b) will or may arise in future." (6): an interim participant
-- is assumed to "become a lifetime participant".
-- (7), (8): a person who "has ceased to be an interim participant" and "has not become a lifetime participant": no damages for
-- needs that "arose during the period in respect of which the person was an interim participant". Future needs are not barred.
-- (10): "This section has effect despite section 12."
-- s 13A is in Part 2 Division 3, which every item of the s 3A Table takes away (cla2-common.l4), and s 6(4) keeps Part 2 off
-- an incident before Part 2 commenced. So a CTP claim, or a worker's claim against the employer, is outside it (the
-- baseline-2026-10 finding 3).
-- "No damages can be awarded": JUST FALSE where the bar bites. Elsewhere s 13A is silent, and s 12 and the general law decide:
-- NOTHING.
@export Can I be awarded damages for my treatment, care and support needs when I am, or was, in the catastrophic injuries support scheme (s 13A)?
GIVEN
    `my injury` IS A `My injury` @desc Is your injury a motor vehicle injury or a workplace injury, as the Motor Vehicle and Workplace Accidents (Catastrophic Injuries) Act 2016 uses those terms, or another injury?
    `my place in the CISS` IS A `My place in the CISS` @desc Where do you stand in the catastrophic injuries support scheme (CISS) for this injury?
    `when the needs arise` IS A `When the care needs arise` @desc When did, or will, the treatment, care and support needs you claim for arise?
    `the class of my damages` IS A `The class of my damages under s 3A` @desc Does your claim fall in a class of the s 3A Table, for example a CTP claim against a driver's insurer or a workers' compensation claim against your employer?
    `the incident was after Part 2 commenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the incident that caused the injury happen after 1 January 2003 (or, if that cannot be known, did symptoms first appear after then)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be awarded damages for my care needs in the CISS` IS
    IF     `Division 3 is taken away by s 3A` `the class of my damages`
        OR `s 6(4) keeps Part 2 out` `the class of my damages` `the incident was after Part 2 commenced`
        OR `my injury` EQUALS `another injury`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `my place in the CISS`
         WHEN `I am a lifetime participant for this injury` THEN `barred while a participant or in future`
         WHEN `I am an interim participant for this injury` THEN `barred while a participant or in future`
         WHEN `I was an interim participant, stopped being one, and did not become a lifetime participant` THEN
             IF `when the needs arise` EQUALS `while I am, or was, a participant`
             THEN JUST FALSE
             ELSE NOTHING
         WHEN `I have never been a participant for this injury` THEN NOTHING
    WHERE
        `barred while a participant or in future` MEANS
            IF `when the needs arise` EQUALS `before I became a participant`
            THEN NOTHING
            ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 14, 15 -- structured settlements`

-- s 14: "structured settlement means an agreement that provides for all or part of the damages agreed or awarded to be paid in
-- the form of periodic payments funded by an annuity or other agreed means." s 15(1): "This section applies if the parties to
-- a claim for personal injury damages make a structured settlement and apply to the court ... for an order approving of, or
-- in the terms of, the structured settlement." (2): "The court may make the order even though the payment of damages is not
-- in the form of a lump sum."
-- s 3A: Division 4 is kept for items 2, 3, 4 and 6 and taken away for items 1 and 5 (NOTHING); s 6(4) for claims in no
-- class. "applies if": JUST FALSE when the parties have not both made the settlement and applied. JUST TRUE means the court
-- can make the order, not that it will.
@export Can the court approve my structured settlement, paid in instalments rather than a lump sum (ss 14, 15)?
GIVEN
    `we agreed periodic payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you and the other party agreed that all or part of your damages will be paid as periodic payments funded by an annuity or other agreed means?
    `we applied to the court for an order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the parties applied to the court for an order approving the settlement, or in its terms?
    `the class of my damages` IS A `The class of my damages under s 3A` @desc Does your claim fall in a class of the s 3A Table, for example a CTP claim or a workers' compensation claim against your employer?
    `the incident was after Part 2 commenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the incident that caused the injury happen after 1 January 2003 (or, if that cannot be known, did symptoms first appear after then)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the court approve my structured settlement` IS
    IF     `Division 4 is taken away by s 3A` `the class of my damages`
        OR `s 6(4) keeps Part 2 out` `the class of my damages` `the incident was after Part 2 commenced`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `we agreed periodic payments` AND `we applied to the court for an order`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE
